        "statement": "Supply a finite polygonal disk-band oriented Seifert surface, its local ambient smooth roundings, and the resulting smooth oriented knot $K=\\partial F\\subset S^3$. Supply a compatible closed product tube $N(K)$, a positive meridian $\\mu$, a preferred zero longitude $\\lambda$ obtained by trimming and paralleling $F$, and peripheral base paths. Put $X_K=S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(K)$ and let $M(K)$ be its zero-longitude filling. Then\n$$H_1(X_K;\\mathbb Z)=\\mathbb Z[\\mu],\\qquad \\lambda\\in\\pi_1(X_K)^{(2)}.$$\nBoth $\\pi_1(X_K)$ and $\\pi_1(M(K))$ are normally generated by their marked meridian images. These conclusions use no choice principle. The finite model and tubes are part of the input; no existence theorem for a neighborhood of an arbitrary locally flat surface is assumed.",
