        "statement": "Let $g\\ge0$ and let $W$ be an integral $2g\\times2g$ matrix satisfying\n$$W-W^T=\\bigoplus_{j=1}^g\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\-1&0\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nA finite construction produces a compact connected smooth oriented surface $F\\subset S^3$ with one boundary component and an ordered basis $a_1,\\ldots,a_{2g}$ of $H_1(F;\\mathbb Z)$ such that\n$$\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)=W_{ij}.$$\nHere $a_i^+$ is a sufficiently small push in the positive oriented normal direction to $F$. The construction uses a finite disk-and-band diagram, finitely many full twists and pairwise clasps, and finite local smoothing. It needs no choice axiom, abstract classification of Seifert forms, generic-projection theorem for arbitrary curves, or normal-neighborhood theorem for locally flat surfaces in four dimensions.",
